{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-review\"","topn":100,"sort":"updated","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\", \"issue_number\": 2653, \"body\": \"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\\npipeline cleanly.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] New session \\u2192 new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) \\u2192 same log file continues\\n- [ ] Session idle >2h \\u2192 next tool call starts a new log file\\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **19. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **20. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\", \"issue_number\": 2551, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\\n\\n## Why\\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\\n\\n## Scope\\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Root hardening: #2546\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"display_title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\", \"issue_number\": 2528, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\\\"12 skills \\u2192 4-5\\\") is partially complete \\u2014 `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\\n\\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\\n\\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\\n\\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\\n\\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n\\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed \\u2014 no broken references to deleted skills\\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable \\u2014 referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\\\"*.md\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.py\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.yaml\\\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\\n\\n## Complexity\\n\\nT1 (trivial) \\u2014 pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"display_title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\", \"issue_number\": 2643, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\\n\\n## Context\\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\\n\\nLive prerequisite checks found:\\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\\n\\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\\n\\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\\n\\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\\n\\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\", \"issue_number\": 2632, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThree llm-wiki issues at `status:plan-approved` (#2368, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125) have been stuck since 2026-04-28 due to a missing/stale approval-binding state. Codex's 10-thread parallel-implementation lanes correctly refused to execute, and the gate has held for 5+ days without remediation. This META issue captures the rot so it can be cleaned up in one pass.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 contract (memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`), `status:plan-approved` GitHub label is necessary but not sufficient \\u2014 execution requires a revision-bound approval marker at `.planning/plan-approved/<n>.md` that names the approved plan SHA + review artifact paths. Otherwise agents can't confirm WHICH version of the plan was approved.\\n\\nThis was specifically designed as a load-bearing user-in-loop gate (memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md`) \\u2014 agents must NOT self-approve by creating the marker themselves.\\n\\nThe gate is doing its job. But the cleanup hasn't happened, and three valuable llm-wiki improvements have been frozen.\\n\\n## Per-issue state (verified 2026-05-03)\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2368.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Local plan `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md`: blob `b391641688` \\u2014 header says `Status: draft` (REGRESSED from v2)\\n- Approved revision per Codex's 2026-04-28 comment: SHA `1c01062d8` \\u2014 header in that SHA says `Status: draft (v2 \\u2014 addresses r1 findings)`, blob `b1df634b3`\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:17:06Z (3 retry passes, all gated)\\n- Likely cause of plan regression: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` pattern during auto-sync\\n\\n**Remediation:**\\n```bash\\ngit checkout 1c01062d8 -- docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md\\n# Then create .planning/plan-approved/2368.md with marker:\\n#   plan_sha: 1c01062d8\\n#   plan_blob: b1df634b3943db8f99888cb120ccf9be6ce245fe\\n#   review_artifacts:\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-claude.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-codex.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-gemini.md\\n#   approved_by: vamseeachanta\\n#   approved_at: <ISO timestamp of human approval>\\ngit add docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md .planning/plan-approved/2368.md\\ngit commit -m \\\"markers(plan-approved): bind vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 to v2 SHA 1c01062d8\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 extend ingestion to Orcina resources/examples/training\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2124.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2124*` exists)\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:18:13Z \\u2014 also flags upstream dependency on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 still being open\\n- Note: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 status as of 2026-05-03 (verify before remediating)\\n\\n**Remediation:** plan needs to be authored or located before binding. May be that the plan was lost to the same merge-race that ate vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22's v2 content.\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 auto-refresh ingestion on Orcina releases\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2125.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2125*` exists)\\n- Codex 2026-04-28T06:15:27Z comment indicates an implementation pass DID complete: branch `codex/10thread-20260428-issue-2125`, commit `e4b6193236a70ed2ec960deb92b3f65b9f876616`. But no merge to main and label still says `status:working`.\\n\\n**Remediation:** check if commit `e4b6193236` is salvageable; either land it or rebind plan + re-execute.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis META issue is for **diagnosis + decision-making**, not implementation:\\n\\n- Confirm the 3 issues' approval-binding state matches what's recorded above (re-verify before acting)\\n- For each: decide rebind / re-plan / archive / continue-as-is\\n- File ONE remediation issue per surviving plan\\n- Update the relevant memory files if the rebinding workflow needs refinement\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- Each of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 reaches one of: (a) properly bound + ready for execution, (b) deferred with explicit ADR, (c) closed as superseded\\n- The meta cleanup commit pattern is documented as a precedent for future \\\"approval-binding rot\\\" sweeps\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Implementation of the 3 issues' actual deliverables (separate downstream work after rebinding)\\n- Codex 10-thread lane reactivation (that's a separate workflow concern)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 (closed) \\u2014 original approval-binding contract; memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`\\n- Memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md` \\u2014 why agents can't self-approve\\n- Memory: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` \\u2014 likely cause of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 plan regression\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 \\u2014 llm-wiki strengthening epic (parent for vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22/#2124/#2125)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2615 (closed 2026-05-03) \\u2014 recent successful approval-binding precedent (Tier C closure)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"display_title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\", \"issue_number\": 2626, \"body\": \"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\\n\\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\\n\\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\\n\\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\\n\\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\\nScenario 3 suggests \\\"temporary lift of interaction limit\\\" \\u2014 globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\\n\\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\\n\\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\\n\\n## Severity\\n\\nMedium \\u2014 the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"display_title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\", \"issue_number\": 2510, \"body\": \"## Context\\nParent: #2507\\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\\n\\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\\n\\n## Proposed scope\\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\\n3. Metadata extraction report.\\n4. Tests and documentation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"display_title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh","issue_number":2653,"body":"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\n\n### Why\n\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\npipeline cleanly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] New session → new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) → same log file continues\n- [ ] Session idle >2h → next tool call starts a new log file\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** — done\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **19. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **20. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","display_title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown","issue_number":2551,"body":"## Summary\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\n\n## Why\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\n\n## Scope\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\n\n## Related\n- Root hardening: #2546\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","display_title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model","issue_number":2528,"body":"## Context\n\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\"12 skills → 4-5\") is partially complete — `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\n\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\n\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\n\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\n\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed — no broken references to deleted skills\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable — referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\"*.md\"` `--include=\"*.py\"` `--include=\"*.yaml\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\n\n## Complexity\n\nT1 (trivial) — pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\n\n## References\n\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","display_title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage","issue_number":2643,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\n\n## Context\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\n\nLive prerequisite checks found:\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\n\n## Problem\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\n\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\n\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\n\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\n\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\n\n## Scope\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\n\n## Out of scope\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","display_title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632","title":"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)","issue_number":2632,"body":"## Summary\n\nThree llm-wiki issues at `status:plan-approved` (#2368, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125) have been stuck since 2026-04-28 due to a missing/stale approval-binding state. Codex's 10-thread parallel-implementation lanes correctly refused to execute, and the gate has held for 5+ days without remediation. This META issue captures the rot so it can be cleaned up in one pass.\n\n## Why\n\nPer the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 contract (memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`), `status:plan-approved` GitHub label is necessary but not sufficient — execution requires a revision-bound approval marker at `.planning/plan-approved/<n>.md` that names the approved plan SHA + review artifact paths. Otherwise agents can't confirm WHICH version of the plan was approved.\n\nThis was specifically designed as a load-bearing user-in-loop gate (memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md`) — agents must NOT self-approve by creating the marker themselves.\n\nThe gate is doing its job. But the cleanup hasn't happened, and three valuable llm-wiki improvements have been frozen.\n\n## Per-issue state (verified 2026-05-03)\n\n### vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2368.md`: **MISSING**\n- Local plan `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md`: blob `b391641688` — header says `Status: draft` (REGRESSED from v2)\n- Approved revision per Codex's 2026-04-28 comment: SHA `1c01062d8` — header in that SHA says `Status: draft (v2 — addresses r1 findings)`, blob `b1df634b3`\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:17:06Z (3 retry passes, all gated)\n- Likely cause of plan regression: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` pattern during auto-sync\n\n**Remediation:**\n```bash\ngit checkout 1c01062d8 -- docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md\n# Then create .planning/plan-approved/2368.md with marker:\n#   plan_sha: 1c01062d8\n#   plan_blob: b1df634b3943db8f99888cb120ccf9be6ce245fe\n#   review_artifacts:\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-claude.md\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-codex.md\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-gemini.md\n#   approved_by: vamseeachanta\n#   approved_at: <ISO timestamp of human approval>\ngit add docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md .planning/plan-approved/2368.md\ngit commit -m \"markers(plan-approved): bind vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 to v2 SHA 1c01062d8\"\n```\n\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 extend ingestion to Orcina resources/examples/training\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2124.md`: **MISSING**\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2124*` exists)\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:18:13Z — also flags upstream dependency on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 still being open\n- Note: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 status as of 2026-05-03 (verify before remediating)\n\n**Remediation:** plan needs to be authored or located before binding. May be that the plan was lost to the same merge-race that ate vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22's v2 content.\n\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 auto-refresh ingestion on Orcina releases\n\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` ✓\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2125.md`: **MISSING**\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2125*` exists)\n- Codex 2026-04-28T06:15:27Z comment indicates an implementation pass DID complete: branch `codex/10thread-20260428-issue-2125`, commit `e4b6193236a70ed2ec960deb92b3f65b9f876616`. But no merge to main and label still says `status:working`.\n\n**Remediation:** check if commit `e4b6193236` is salvageable; either land it or rebind plan + re-execute.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis META issue is for **diagnosis + decision-making**, not implementation:\n\n- Confirm the 3 issues' approval-binding state matches what's recorded above (re-verify before acting)\n- For each: decide rebind / re-plan / archive / continue-as-is\n- File ONE remediation issue per surviving plan\n- Update the relevant memory files if the rebinding workflow needs refinement\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Each of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 reaches one of: (a) properly bound + ready for execution, (b) deferred with explicit ADR, (c) closed as superseded\n- The meta cleanup commit pattern is documented as a precedent for future \"approval-binding rot\" sweeps\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Implementation of the 3 issues' actual deliverables (separate downstream work after rebinding)\n- Codex 10-thread lane reactivation (that's a separate workflow concern)\n\n## References\n\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 (closed) — original approval-binding contract; memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`\n- Memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md` — why agents can't self-approve\n- Memory: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` — likely cause of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 plan regression\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 — llm-wiki strengthening epic (parent for vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22/#2124/#2125)\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2615 (closed 2026-05-03) — recent successful approval-binding precedent (Tier C closure)\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632","display_title":"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction","issue_number":2626,"body":"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\n\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\n\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\n\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\n\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\nScenario 3 suggests \"temporary lift of interaction limit\" — globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\n\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\n\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\n\n## Severity\n\nMedium — the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626","display_title":"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 — drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries","issue_number":2510,"body":"## Context\nParent: #2507\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\n\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\n\n## Proposed scope\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\n\n## Deliverables\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\n3. Metadata extraction report.\n4. Tests and documentation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","display_title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
