{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:blocked\"","topn":100,"sort":"updated","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\", \"issue_number\": 2269, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\\n\\nPart of #1782.\\nPrimary reference: #25.\\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\\n\\n## Motivation\\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\\n\\nExpected deliverables:\\n- baseline docs\\n- run/validation entrypoints\\n- minimal smoke example\\n- troubleshooting guidance\\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\\n\\n## Notes\\nImplementation should prefer:\\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269\", \"display_title\": \"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\", \"issue_number\": 2402, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR\\u00d72 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\\n\\n## Deliverable\\n\\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model \\u00a77 \\u2014 **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model \\u00a73).\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per \\u00a73 \\u2014 enforced and tested\\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s \\u2014 measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n\\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) \\u2014 live in their own issues.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402\", \"display_title\": \"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152\", \"title\": \"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage\", \"issue_number\": 2152, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAdd the golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage.\\n\\n## Why\\nValidator and renderer work need stable example artifacts representing healthy, degraded, and invalid runs. Fixtures also flush out schema ambiguities early.\\n\\n## Scope\\n- add valid weekly-review run artifact fixtures for minimal, full, degraded, and multi-machine runs\\n- add invalid fixtures for missing keys, bad enums, bad timestamps, and malformed sections\\n- define expected validator outcomes for invalid cases\\n- document fixture naming and refresh rules\\n- wire fixtures into validator CI tests\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- valid and invalid fixture corpus\\n- expected validator outputs\\n- fixture README\\n- CI test usage\\n\\n## Parent\\n- Parent issues: #2146, #2147, #2089\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152\", \"display_title\": \"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation","issue_number":2269,"body":"## Summary\nStandardize the canonical OpenFOAM baseline for portable engineering work, using repo-tracked docs, scripts, example cases, and validation.\n\nPart of #1782.\nPrimary reference: #25.\nSupports downstream work such as #1268.\n\n## Motivation\nOpenFOAM is already CLI-native, but the baseline workflow is not yet fully encoded as a portable artifact bundle. We need a declared version target, canonical entrypoints, and a smoke validation path.\n\n## Scope\nCreate the baseline OpenFOAM portability package in workspace-hub.\n\nExpected deliverables:\n- baseline docs\n- run/validation entrypoints\n- minimal smoke example\n- troubleshooting guidance\n- shared skill update if reusable guidance is improved\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] baseline doc declares the target fork/version explicitly (default: ESI/OpenFOAM.com v2312 unless changed by decision)\n- [ ] canonical runner command(s) are documented\n- [ ] minimal smoke case exists under a reproducible repo-tracked path\n- [ ] validator produces pass/fail output with explicit checks\n- [ ] common failure modes and version/fork mismatches are documented\n- [ ] workflow can be executed on the canonical engineering host with documented prerequisites\n\n## Notes\nImplementation should prefer:\n- explicit version detection and fail-fast behavior\n- repo-tracked wrappers over tribal command memory\n- logs/results/validation outputs in predictable locations\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2269","display_title":"feat(openfoam): standardize ESI v2312 baseline workflow and validation"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)","issue_number":2402,"body":"## Context\n\nSplit from vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2393 (v1 closed after MAJOR×2 cross-provider review flagged scope creep + storage-authority ambiguity + AC-vs-test gaps).\n\n## Problem\n\nBuild the actual embeddings index using the model chosen in vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403. This issue focuses on build + query, with a resolved single-authority storage tier.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n- Build script: `scripts/knowledge/build_embeddings_index.py` (incremental, idempotent).\n- Query CLI: `scripts/knowledge/query_embeddings.py`.\n- Storage: single authoritative tier per operating-model §7 — **decided in plan**, not left ambiguous.\n- Manifest (git-tracked): `data/document-index/embeddings-manifest.yaml`.\n- `sha256:`-only `doc_key` enforcement at build and query time (per operating-model §3).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All doc_keys in the index validated as `sha256:<hex>` per §3 — enforced and tested\n- [ ] Single authoritative storage tier declared in plan (repo-local OR shared-mount, not both)\n- [ ] p95 query latency < 2s — measured via `tests/knowledge/test_query_latency.py` (not manual)\n- [ ] Row-count + model-pin + refresh-timestamp in `embeddings-manifest.yaml`\n- [ ] Cost-cap guardrail has a concrete implementing file + test\n- [ ] Nightly cron wired in `config/scheduled-tasks/schedule-tasks.yaml`\n- [ ] Threat model section: cloud-API secret sourcing, mount-path validation, cache-poisoning protection\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- **Hard depends on: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2403** (model choice must be made first)\n- Depends on: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#23 (`doc_key` in wiki frontmatter), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2361, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2362\n- Blocks: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2394 (retrieval-augmented planner), vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2400 (MCP wiki_search tool)\n\n## Scope boundaries\n\n- **In scope:** build, query, manifest, cost-cap, cron, secrets, threat model.\n- **Out of scope:** downstream consumers (planner, MCP server) — live in their own issues.","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2402","display_title":"feat(doc-intel): build embeddings index L2+L3 + query CLI (single authoritative tier)"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152","title":"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage","issue_number":2152,"body":"## Summary\nAdd the golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage.\n\n## Why\nValidator and renderer work need stable example artifacts representing healthy, degraded, and invalid runs. Fixtures also flush out schema ambiguities early.\n\n## Scope\n- add valid weekly-review run artifact fixtures for minimal, full, degraded, and multi-machine runs\n- add invalid fixtures for missing keys, bad enums, bad timestamps, and malformed sections\n- define expected validator outcomes for invalid cases\n- document fixture naming and refresh rules\n- wire fixtures into validator CI tests\n\n## Deliverables\n- valid and invalid fixture corpus\n- expected validator outputs\n- fixture README\n- CI test usage\n\n## Parent\n- Parent issues: #2146, #2147, #2089\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2152","display_title":"test(reporting): add golden fixture corpus for weekly review run artifacts and validator coverage"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
