{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-approved\" created:>=2026-05-01","topn":100,"sort":"created","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\", \"issue_number\": 2657, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\\n\\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessions\\n- Rolling 7d activity: 9,083 post records / 403 sessions\\n- Audit status: `health=red`, `tier=next_up`, `primary issue=llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`\\n- Corpus interpretation: `positive_corpus_growth_beyond_recent_activity`; treat as event-time work plus export/classification interpretation, not as a pure recent-work count.\\n\\n## Top recent Hermes surfaces\\n\\nReads:\\n- `business.gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel.digitalmodel-code-explorer`\\n- `github.github-issues`\\n- `gtm-parametric-demo-reports`\\n- `digitalmodel/docs/plans/2026-05-07-issue-596-repo-structure-normalization.md`\\n\\nWrites/edits included digitalmodel GTM planning/demo artifacts and vessel-suitability references. The audit's remediation target remains llm-wiki spinout path drift, not the GTM artifacts themselves.\\n\\n## Required plan-before-implementation scope\\n\\nBefore implementation, produce a plan that:\\n\\n1. Samples the audit's top stale llm-wiki paths, especially:\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/engineering/wiki/log.md`\\n   - `knowledge/wikis/marine-engineering/wiki/index.md`\\n2. Decides whether each path should be redirected, documented as an intentional historical path, or removed from prompts/tools.\\n3. Updates canonical targets only after plan approval:\\n   - `llm-wiki/wikis/`\\n   - `llm-wiki/docs/`\\n   - `docs/session-handoffs/2026-05-05-llm-wiki-spinout-max-completeness-handoff.md`\\n4. Preserves the distinction between event-time activity and corpus/snapshot growth.\\n5. Adds provider-session audit tests if script classification changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- No new hardcoded `knowledge/wikis/.../wiki/` stale spinout references remain in active prompts/docs/tools unless explicitly documented as historical evidence.\\n- Provider-session audit still passes after remediation.\\n- Follow-up report or issue comment includes before/after evidence for sampled stale paths.\\n- GitHub issue remains in planning workflow until user approval; no implementation before plan approval.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657\", \"display_title\": \"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\", \"issue_number\": 2656, \"body\": \"## Objective\\n\\nPlan a conservative, repo-by-repo folder/file structure normalization for `workspace-hub` under the workspace-hub tier-1 ecosystem workflow.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nPlanning only until explicit user approval. The plan must inventory current structure, identify root clutter/generated-output risk, propose a bounded Phase 1 refactor contract, define TDD/verification gates, and preserve evidence needed for rollback.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n- Canonical plan artifact under `docs/plans/`.\\n- Review artifact under `scripts/review/results/`.\\n- Final issue comment linking the plan and review artifact.\\n\\n## Approval Gate\\n\\nNo file moves, package reorganization, deletion, or cleanup execution is authorized until this issue is explicitly approved after plan review.\\n\\nParent ecosystem anchors: `workspace-hub#1962`, `workspace-hub#2397`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2656\", \"display_title\": \"chore(repo-structure): normalize workspace-hub folder/file structure\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2628\", \"title\": \"epic(digitalmodel-ci): domain-divided CI architecture replacing maxfail-masking pattern\", \"issue_number\": 2628, \"body\": \"## Why now\\n\\nThis session surfaced that digitalmodel's QG suite has been chronically green-washed by \\\\`maxfail=20\\\\` masking 200+ pre-existing failures across 53 test files. The admin-merge-via-Quality-Gates-failure pattern (PRs [#541](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/541), [#544](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/544), [#549](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/549), [#550](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/550), [#551](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/551), [#553](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/553), [#568](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/568), [#569](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/569)) is now the default merge path \\u2014 operationally fast but strategically corrosive: every PR carries the same 'gate trips on unrelated debt' justification.\\n\\nRoot cause: a single repo-wide \\\\`pytest --maxfail=20\\\\` invocation can't distinguish 'this PR introduced a regression in its own scope' from 'unrelated debt elsewhere in the repo.' Per-domain CI fixes both.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n**14-15 test domains** (per [#2616](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2616) sweep + tests/ tree):\\n\\n\\\\`asset_integrity\\\\`, \\\\`citations\\\\`, \\\\`contracts\\\\`, \\\\`field_development\\\\`, \\\\`hydrodynamics-diffraction\\\\`, \\\\`hydrodynamics-passing-ship\\\\`, \\\\`infrastructure-core\\\\`, \\\\`marine-engineering\\\\`, \\\\`naval-architecture\\\\`, \\\\`orcaflex\\\\`, \\\\`orcaflex-solver\\\\`, \\\\`solver-smoke\\\\`, \\\\`specialized\\\\`, \\\\`structural\\\\`, \\\\`workflows\\\\`, \\\\`misc\\\\`\\n\\nEach domain becomes:\\n- a separate pytest job in a GH Actions matrix\\n- with its own \\\\`--with\\\\` dep list (so e.g. redis/psycopg2/motor only attach to \\\\`infrastructure-core\\\\`, not the whole CI)\\n- with its own conftest fixtures and skipif policies\\n- with the existing \\\\`maxfail\\\\` removed (per-domain failure counts stay bounded by domain size)\\n\\n## Decisions locked (this session, vamseeachanta)\\n\\n| Decision | Choice |\\n|---|---|\\n| Domain owner | All domains owned by \\\\`vamseeachanta\\\\` (single owner; CODEOWNERS encodes this) |\\n| Aggregator gate policy | **All domains must pass** for merge (no informational-only mode) |\\n| Run cadence | **Touched-domains-only on PRs**; **full matrix nightly** (cron) |\\n| Deprecation policy | No test deletion or blanket-skip without AI-attested 'source X is gone, no other consumers' commit per \\\\`feedback_attestation_enables_contradiction_detection\\\\` |\\n\\n## Sub-tasks\\n\\n- [ ] **A** \\u2014 Domain inventory PR (\\\\`tests/DOMAINS.md\\\\` mapping every test directory \\u2192 domain \\u2192 dep set; informs all subsequent PRs). Read-only repo analysis. \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **B** \\u2014 \\\\`.claude/quality-gates.yaml\\\\` refactor: one gate per domain with its own command + deps. Aggregator gate depends on all. Drops repo-wide \\\\`maxfail\\\\`. \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **C** \\u2014 GH Actions matrix workflow: \\\\`.github/workflows/quality-gates-by-domain.yml\\\\` with \\\\`strategy.matrix.domain\\\\` for parallel runs + aggregator job. \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **D** \\u2014 Touched-domain detection: PR-time job that diffs changed paths against \\\\`tests/DOMAINS.md\\\\` and emits the matrix subset to run. Nightly cron uses full matrix. \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **E** \\u2014 Per-domain conftest extraction: move shared fixtures/skipifs from \\\\`tests/conftest.py\\\\` into each domain's local conftest. ~1 PR per domain (small each). \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **F** \\u2014 CODEOWNERS file with \\\\`vamseeachanta\\\\` as default owner. \\\\`digitalmodel\\\\`.\\n- [ ] **G** \\u2014 Update workspace-hub agents.md + CLAUDE.md to encode the 'always test by domain during development' rule for AI agents. \\\\`workspace-hub\\\\`.\\n\\n## After A-G land, the deferred cluster work re-routes by domain\\n\\n| Cluster | Issue | New domain home |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| A \\u2014 sys.modules pollution | [#2623](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2623) | \\\\`contracts\\\\` domain |\\n| D \\u2014 infrastructure dep wall | [#2624](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2624) | \\\\`infrastructure-core\\\\` domain \\u2014 its own \\\\`--with redis --with psycopg2-binary --with motor\\\\` |\\n| E \\u2014 marine-engineering regressions | [#2625](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2625) | \\\\`marine-engineering\\\\` domain \\u2014 its own targeted suite |\\n\\nThese clusters become much cheaper to fix per-domain than under repo-wide CI.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Domain inventory exists and is reviewable\\n- [ ] PR for trivial change (e.g. docs typo) only runs domains that own changed paths; runs in <2 min\\n- [ ] PR that touches multiple domains runs all touched domains; aggregator gates correctly\\n- [ ] Nightly full matrix runs all domains; failure surfaces per-domain in GH Actions UI\\n- [ ] No test files deleted as part of this work; debt that surfaces is filed per-domain for owner triage\\n- [ ] Existing admin-merge cycle ends \\u2014 next post-A-G PR merges through the new gate without override\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n- [#2614](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2614), [#2616](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2616) \\u2014 investigations that surfaced the masking\\n- [#2129](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2129) \\u2014 issue-state drift / quality-gates audit umbrella\\n- [vamseeachanta/digitalmodel#543](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/digitalmodel/pull/543) \\u2014 PR that introduced \\\\`maxfail=20\\\\`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2628\", \"display_title\": \"epic(digitalmodel-ci): domain-divided CI architecture replacing maxfail-masking pattern\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2657","title":"chore(provider-session): remediate Hermes llm-wiki spinout path drift","issue_number":2657,"body":"## Summary\n\nThe refreshed provider-session audit (`2026-05-08T11:03:24Z`) escalated Hermes to a red/next-up remediation lane for `llm_wiki_spinout_path_drift`.\n\nDurable transfer report: `docs/reports/2026-05-08-provider-session-learning-transfer.md`.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Previous audit boundary: `2026-05-07T09:37:54Z`\n- Recent Hermes event-time activity: 1,857 post-hook records / 70 runtime sessions\n- Rolling 24h activity: 828 post records / 36 sessio