{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-review\" created:>=2026-05-01","topn":100,"sort":"created","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\", \"issue_number\": 2643, \"body\": \"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\\n\\n## Context\\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\\n\\nLive prerequisite checks found:\\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392 is the coverage-gap detector issue, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487 already delivered the raw-data-to-readiness spine/control-plane.\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe raw-like mounted source estate is not yet consistently classified into:\\n1. llm-wiki/document-intelligence candidates,\\n2. existing/in-flight coverage,\\n3. code/vendor/internal exclusions,\\n4. private/project-sensitive exclusions, and\\n5. future source-family package candidates requiring separate approval.\\n\\nWithout this metadata-only triage layer, agents risk either missing high-value source families or over-promoting raw/private/project data into git/wiki.\\n\\n## Metadata-only inventory evidence\\nRepresentative discovered raw-like directories:\\n\\n| Source path | Metadata-only count | Initial routing |\\n|---|---:|---|\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/O&G-Standards/raw` | 28,803 files / 692 dirs | standards candidate, reconcile with vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/#2392/#2487 and completed bounded standards promotions |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/client_projects/energy_bsee/raw_data` | 10 files | offshore/BSEE candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/aqwa/data/scripts/mooring_analysis/raw` | 28 files | AQWA candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/digitalmodel/docs/orcaflex/literature/examples/raw` | 38 files / 76 dirs | OrcaFlex examples candidate; map to vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 rather than duplicate |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/frontierdeepwater/data/raw` | 4 files / 1 dir | offshore source candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/worldenergydata/data/modules/hse/raw` | 97 files / 7 dirs | HSE/safety data candidate; no direct duplicate issue found |\\n| `/mnt/ace-data/docs/disciplines/misc/projects/0136_das/.../Data/Raw` | 215 files / 8 dirs | indexed as `acma-projects`/project-management gap; project-sensitive until separately approved |\\n\\nNon-corpus/exclusion examples include empty `.gitkeep` raw dirs, Rust crate internals, Struts image assets, QGIS generated DXF output, SSI marketing images, OPM parser source internals, and similar code/vendor/generated/personal/project-sensitive surfaces.\\n\\n## Scope\\nCreate a canonical plan for a metadata-only raw-like source triage and routing artifact. The plan should:\\n- preserve the raw-data boundary: no copying/promoting raw content to git/wiki;\\n- classify discovered raw-like roots by source family, sensitivity, target wiki/domain, existing issue mapping, and recommended next action;\\n- update or define a durable metadata/routing artifact under the document-intelligence surface;\\n- link resulting source-family work back to vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487;\\n- identify which families need separate follow-up issues before any summary promotion.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n- No raw data import into git/wiki.\\n- No direct llm-wiki page generation from raw documents in this issue.\\n- No standards content extraction from proprietary/copyrighted documents.\\n- No project-sensitive corpus promotion (SESA/Woodfibre/ACMA/DAS/client material) without separate explicit approval.\\n- No implementation before canonical plan review and user approval.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] A canonical plan is created under `docs/plans/` and indexed in `docs/plans/README.md`.\\n- [ ] The plan cites the metadata-only inventory, `data/document-index/mounted-source-registry.yaml`, `data/document-index/index.jsonl`, `docs/document-intelligence/data-intelligence-map.md`, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2392, and vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2487.\\n- [ ] The plan includes a raw-like source routing matrix covering all discovered raw-like roots.\\n- [ ] Existing/in-flight issue mappings are explicit: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2103 for AQWA, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 for OrcaFlex examples, vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#25/#2373/standards wave issues for O&G standards, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2540/#2541-#2544/#2559 for Elements-derived material.\\n- [ ] The final plan-review comment requests user approval and labels this issue `status:plan-review`.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643\", \"display_title\": \"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\", \"issue_number\": 2632, \"body\": \"## Summary\\n\\nThree llm-wiki issues at `status:plan-approved` (#2368, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125) have been stuck since 2026-04-28 due to a missing/stale approval-binding state. Codex's 10-thread parallel-implementation lanes correctly refused to execute, and the gate has held for 5+ days without remediation. This META issue captures the rot so it can be cleaned up in one pass.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nPer the vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 contract (memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`), `status:plan-approved` GitHub label is necessary but not sufficient \\u2014 execution requires a revision-bound approval marker at `.planning/plan-approved/<n>.md` that names the approved plan SHA + review artifact paths. Otherwise agents can't confirm WHICH version of the plan was approved.\\n\\nThis was specifically designed as a load-bearing user-in-loop gate (memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md`) \\u2014 agents must NOT self-approve by creating the marker themselves.\\n\\nThe gate is doing its job. But the cleanup hasn't happened, and three valuable llm-wiki improvements have been frozen.\\n\\n## Per-issue state (verified 2026-05-03)\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 faceted portal pages for large LLM-wiki domains\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2368.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Local plan `docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md`: blob `b391641688` \\u2014 header says `Status: draft` (REGRESSED from v2)\\n- Approved revision per Codex's 2026-04-28 comment: SHA `1c01062d8` \\u2014 header in that SHA says `Status: draft (v2 \\u2014 addresses r1 findings)`, blob `b1df634b3`\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:17:06Z (3 retry passes, all gated)\\n- Likely cause of plan regression: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` pattern during auto-sync\\n\\n**Remediation:**\\n```bash\\ngit checkout 1c01062d8 -- docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md\\n# Then create .planning/plan-approved/2368.md with marker:\\n#   plan_sha: 1c01062d8\\n#   plan_blob: b1df634b3943db8f99888cb120ccf9be6ce245fe\\n#   review_artifacts:\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-claude.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-codex.md\\n#     - scripts/review/results/2026-04-23-plan-2368-gemini.md\\n#   approved_by: vamseeachanta\\n#   approved_at: <ISO timestamp of human approval>\\ngit add docs/plans/2026-04-23-issue-2368-faceted-portal-pages.md .planning/plan-approved/2368.md\\ngit commit -m \\\"markers(plan-approved): bind vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 to v2 SHA 1c01062d8\\\"\\n```\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124 extend ingestion to Orcina resources/examples/training\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2124.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2124*` exists)\\n- Codex blocker comment: 2026-04-28T09:18:13Z \\u2014 also flags upstream dependency on vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 still being open\\n- Note: vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2471 status as of 2026-05-03 (verify before remediating)\\n\\n**Remediation:** plan needs to be authored or located before binding. May be that the plan was lost to the same merge-race that ate vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22's v2 content.\\n\\n### vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 auto-refresh ingestion on Orcina releases\\n\\n- GH labels: `status:plan-approved,status:working,agent:codex` \\u2713\\n- `.planning/plan-approved/2125.md`: **MISSING**\\n- Plan file: **MISSING** entirely (no `docs/plans/*2125*` exists)\\n- Codex 2026-04-28T06:15:27Z comment indicates an implementation pass DID complete: branch `codex/10thread-20260428-issue-2125`, commit `e4b6193236a70ed2ec960deb92b3f65b9f876616`. But no merge to main and label still says `status:working`.\\n\\n**Remediation:** check if commit `e4b6193236` is salvageable; either land it or rebind plan + re-execute.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nThis META issue is for **diagnosis + decision-making**, not implementation:\\n\\n- Confirm the 3 issues' approval-binding state matches what's recorded above (re-verify before acting)\\n- For each: decide rebind / re-plan / archive / continue-as-is\\n- File ONE remediation issue per surviving plan\\n- Update the relevant memory files if the rebinding workflow needs refinement\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- Each of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2124, vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2125 reaches one of: (a) properly bound + ready for execution, (b) deferred with explicit ADR, (c) closed as superseded\\n- The meta cleanup commit pattern is documented as a precedent for future \\\"approval-binding rot\\\" sweeps\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Implementation of the 3 issues' actual deliverables (separate downstream work after rebinding)\\n- Codex 10-thread lane reactivation (that's a separate workflow concern)\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2460 (closed) \\u2014 original approval-binding contract; memory: `project_issue_2460_approval_binding.md`\\n- Memory: `feedback_never_offer_to_self_label_plan_approved.md` \\u2014 why agents can't self-approve\\n- Memory: `feedback_merge_race_silent_revert.md` \\u2014 likely cause of vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22 plan regression\\n- vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 \\u2014 llm-wiki strengthening epic (parent for vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#22/#2124/#2125)\\n- vamseeachanta/workspace-hub#2615 (closed 2026-05-03) \\u2014 recent successful approval-binding precedent (Tier C closure)\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2632\", \"display_title\": \"META: rebind 3 llm-wiki plan-approved issues stuck on missing approval markers (#2368/#2124/#2125)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\", \"issue_number\": 2626, \"body\": \"**Source:** #2552 plan-review queue audit 2026-05-03. Per [#2552 approval marker](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/.planning/plan-approved/2552.md), the runbook content was approved despite a 4+ day Tier-D persistent-MAJOR pattern (claude/codex/gemini all MAJOR across 4+ rounds). The architectural defects under those MAJORs are deferred here for a focused fresh plan.\\n\\n## Defects to address (from latest reviews)\\n\\n### 1. Privacy-leaking test (Gemini, repeat)\\nThe proposed `test_runbook_references_triggering_issues_without_personal_name` requires hardcoding the external commenter's PII into the test file to assert its absence. **Resolution:** drop the negative-presence assertion; only positively assert presence of issue numbers (#2401, #2546, #2550).\\n\\n### 2. Undefined ingestion vector under `collaborators_only` lockdown (Gemini, repeat)\\nPlan tells operators to reply via `CONTRIBUTOR_INTEREST_TEMPLATE` but #2546's `collaborators_only` lockdown blocks the input channel. **Resolution:** explicitly define the ingestion vector (likely email or a designated public form) since GitHub interactions are blocked.\\n\\n### 3. Security-posture contradiction in scenario 3 (Gemini, repeat)\\nScenario 3 suggests \\\"temporary lift of interaction limit\\\" \\u2014 globally undermines #2546's lockdown for one request. **Resolution:** either (a) drop scenario 3 entirely from in-scope work, or (b) define a per-user allowlist mechanism that doesn't lift the global limit.\\n\\n### 4. Plan-internal contradictions (Claude, repeat)\\n- Untestable acceptance criteria (negative-presence checks for arbitrary unspecified strings)\\n- HTML-comment metadata contradicts surrounding table (plan was patched in layers without re-reading itself)\\n\\n**Resolution:** restart from a clean T1 spec; do not iterate on the existing plan.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n\\n- [ ] New plan filed under `docs/plans/` addressing items 1-4 explicitly\\n- [ ] Plan goes through one Claude+Gemini review cycle (Codex skipped per #2479 unless version-pin lands first)\\n- [ ] No regression on the runbook content already approved via #2552\\n\\n## Severity\\n\\nMedium \\u2014 the runbook content is live (approved); this issue prevents drift between the runbook and its enforcement layer.\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2626\", \"display_title\": \"fix(security): narrow #2552 external-contributor runbook tests + scenario 3 \\u2014 drop privacy-leaking test, define ingestion vector, resolve interaction-limit contradiction\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2643","title":"feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage","issue_number":2643,"body":"# feat(llm-wiki): plan metadata-only /mnt/ace-data raw-like source coverage triage\n\n## Context\nA user requested extending llm-wiki completion from raw data to llm-wiki completeness for `/mnt/ace-data/raw data`.\n\nLive prerequisite checks found:\n- `/mnt/ace-data` resolves to `/mnt/ace`.\n- The exact literal path `/mnt/ace-data/raw data` does **not** exist.\n- Metadata-only discovery found 14 raw-like directories under `/mnt/ace-data` (`raw`, `raw_data`, or `Raw`), with no raw content copied into git/wiki.\n- Existing overlap must be preserved: vamseeachanta/llm-wiki#13 is the llm-wiki roadmap anchor, vamseeachanta/workspace-hu