{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-review\" created:<2026-05-01","topn":100,"sort":"created","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\", \"issue_number\": 2551, \"body\": \"## Summary\\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\\n\\n## Why\\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\\n\\n## Scope\\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\\n\\n## Related\\n- Root hardening: #2546\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551\", \"display_title\": \"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\", \"issue_number\": 2528, \"body\": \"## Context\\n\\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\\\"12 skills \\u2192 4-5\\\") is partially complete \\u2014 `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\\n\\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\\n\\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\\n\\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\\n\\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\\n\\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n\\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed \\u2014 no broken references to deleted skills\\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable \\u2014 referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\\\"*.md\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.py\\\"` `--include=\\\"*.yaml\\\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\\n\\n## Complexity\\n\\nT1 (trivial) \\u2014 pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\\n\\n## References\\n\\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528\", \"display_title\": \"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\", \"issue_number\": 2510, \"body\": \"## Context\\nParent: #2507\\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\\n\\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\\n\\n## Proposed scope\\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\\n3. Metadata extraction report.\\n4. Tests and documentation.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\\n\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510\", \"display_title\": \"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries\"}, {\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\", \"issue_number\": 2653, \"body\": \"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### What\\n\\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\\npipeline cleanly.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] New session \\u2192 new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) \\u2192 same log file continues\\n- [ ] Session idle >2h \\u2192 next tool call starts a new log file\\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\n- [x] **1. Capture** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **3. Triage** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** \\u2014 done\\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** \\u2014 done\\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** \\u2014 n\\n- [ ] **19. Close** \\u2014 pending\\n- [ ] **20. Archive** \\u2014 pending\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown","issue_number":2551,"body":"## Summary\nAudit public repository rulesets, branch protection, issue/PR permissions, and contributor surfaces after the interaction-limit lockdown in #2546.\n\n## Why\n`collaborators_only` interaction limits reduce public issue/PR/comment noise, but they are temporary and do not replace branch protection / repository rulesets. We need a separate governance pass to ensure code and PR paths are protected consistently across public repos.\n\n## Scope\nFor every active public `vamseeachanta/*` repo:\n- Inventory default branch, branch protection, repository rulesets, required reviews, status checks, and force-push/delete settings.\n- Inventory whether Issues, Discussions, Projects, Wiki, and Actions are enabled and whether each surface is intentional.\n- Identify repos that should be archived, private, or have Issues disabled entirely.\n- Recommend a minimum public-repo protection baseline for code/PR changes.\n- Produce an evidence table and follow-up implementation plan; do not silently mutate branch protection without explicit approval because it can block active workflows.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Public repo table includes: visibility, archived state, default branch, interaction limit status, branch/ruleset status, Issues/PR surfaces.\n- [ ] Findings separate already-hardened interaction limits from code-path protections.\n- [ ] Recommended baseline distinguishes active Tier-1 repos from archived/static repos.\n- [ ] Any proposed branch protection/ruleset changes are drafted as explicit plan-approved follow-up work.\n\n## Related\n- Root hardening: #2546\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2551","display_title":"audit(security): verify branch/ruleset protections across public repos after collaborator-only lockdown"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model","issue_number":2528,"body":"## Context\n\nSupersedes [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019). That issue's scope (\"12 skills → 4-5\") is partially complete — `gmail-extract-and-act` and `gmail-outreach` were created during prior consolidation work, and [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (closed 2026-04-27) created `_archived/` snapshots of 4 deprecated skills. The original plan would re-discover and re-do that work.\n\nThis issue scopes only the **remaining residue**.\n\n## Resource intel (live evidence as of 2026-04-27)\n\nActive skill count under `.claude/skills/email/`: **14** (issue #2019 claimed 12).\n\n| Skill (active) | State | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `gmail-multi-account` | Active, foundation | KEEP |\n| `gmail-triage` | Active, **encodes archive-everything model** | UPDATE to queue model per `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` |\n| `gmail-extract-and-act` | Active, queue-model skill | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-outreach` | Active, merger of touchbase+unsubscribe | KEEP (created during prior consolidation) |\n| `gmail-attachment-to-document` | Active, specialized | KEEP |\n| `gmail-headless-oauth` | Active, infra utility | KEEP |\n| `himalaya` | Active, CLI reference | KEEP |\n| `contact-manager` | Active, CRM data | KEEP |\n| `gmail-touchbase` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-unsubscribe` | Active **AND superseded by gmail-outreach** | **DELETE** |\n| `gmail-data-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-and-clean` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-extract-archive` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n| `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction` | Active **AND has `_archived/` twin** | **DELETE active copy** |\n\nTarget active count after this issue: **8 skills**.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] 6 deprecated skill folders deleted: `gmail-touchbase`, `gmail-unsubscribe`, `gmail-data-extraction`, `gmail-extract-and-clean`, `gmail-extract-archive`, `gmail-email-to-repo-extraction`\n- [ ] `_archived/` versions retained for the 4 that have twins (do not touch `_archived/`)\n- [ ] `gmail-triage` SKILL.md content updated to reference the queue model (not archive model); cross-link `gmail-extract-and-act`\n- [ ] `related_skills:` frontmatter in remaining 8 skills refreshed — no broken references to deleted skills\n- [ ] `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md` Skills table refreshed to reflect 8 active + 4 archived (and remove the DEPRECATED rows for the 4 that no longer exist)\n- [ ] Document state-label naming convention (`wh-email/extracted`, `wh-email/awaiting-reply`, `wh-email/completed`, `wh-email/noise`) somewhere durable — referenced by [#2017 v9 plan line 253](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/blob/main/docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md) as a #2019 deliverable; this is the doc handoff for the future Gmail-mirror v2\n- [ ] No callsite breakage: grep `--include=\"*.md\"` `--include=\"*.py\"` `--include=\"*.yaml\"` for the 6 deleted skill names returns only `_archived/` paths and historical state files\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Building/changing `gmail-extract-and-act` or `gmail-outreach` content (they exist; their internal correctness is `gmail-triage`-update-adjacent but not part of this issue)\n- Any Gmail mutation work (that lives in [#2423](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2423), which is gated on [#2527](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2527) OAuth scope-bump)\n- Per-domain extraction templates (that's [#2024](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2024))\n\n## Complexity\n\nT1 (trivial) — pure file deletions, content edits, and grep verification. Adversarial review optional per issue-planning-mode rules; single-author plan + verification sweep is sufficient.\n\n## References\n\n- Superseded: [#2019](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2019)\n- Sibling closed: [#2488](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2488) (skill-file reconciliation)\n- Parent epic: [#2017](https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2017) (Email-as-Queue workflow)\n- v9 plan: `docs/plans/2026-04-20-issue-2017-plan.md` (line 253: state-label naming doc owner = this issue)\n- WORKFLOW: `docs/email/WORKFLOW.md`\n- Filter runbook (companion): `docs/email/2026-04-27-filter-installation-runbook.md`","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2528","display_title":"chore(skills): retire 6 deprecated email skills + update gmail-triage to queue model"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries","issue_number":2510,"body":"## Context\nParent: #2507\nRoadmap: `docs/roadmaps/chip-design-cad-fem-career-roadmap.md`\n\nBuild a Python-first geometry/layout automation example that bridges CAD practices into semiconductor layout and package/interposer-style structures.\n\n## Proposed scope\n- Use KLayout scripting and/or GDSFactory to generate a parameterized layout artifact.\n- Export/import GDS/OASIS and at least one human-inspectable representation such as SVG/DXF where practical.\n- Extract metadata: layers, polygons, bounding boxes, ports/nets where available, geometry invariants.\n- Include tests around geometry invariants and repeatability.\n\n## Deliverables\n1. Python module/script for parameterized layout generation.\n2. Sample output artifacts or reproducible generation command.\n3. Metadata extraction report.\n4. Tests and documentation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Demo can be run locally without proprietary tools.\n- Generated artifacts are deterministic enough for tests or snapshot checks.\n- Report explains relevance to chip design, packaging, and CAD automation roles.\n","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2510","display_title":"feat(cad): build Python layout/CAD automation demo for chip/package geometries"},{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh","issue_number":2653,"body":"## WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh\n\n\n\n**Status:** Stage 18: Reclaim (n) | **Priority:** medium | **Category:** engineering | **Subcategory:** pipeline\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** simple | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### What\n\nModify `.claude/hooks/session-logger.sh` so each Claude session gets its own\nlog file instead of merging all activity for the day into one file.\n\n### Why\n\nWhen multiple sessions run on the same day (or across a long session), the\ncurrent `session_YYYYMMDD.jsonl` file merges all tool calls into one file.\nPer-session files make it easier to correlate log entries with a specific\nconversation, debug session issues, and feed individual sessions into the RAG\npipeline cleanly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] New session → new log file with `session_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` name\n- [ ] Resumed session (within 2h) → same log file continues\n- [ ] Session idle >2h → next tool call starts a new log file\n- [ ] Both log paths (state/sessions/ and logs/orchestrator/claude/) use the session ID\n- [ ] State file is gitignored (already under `.claude/state/` which is gitignored)\n- [ ] Hook remains <1s execution time (raw-write only principle)\n- [ ] Existing date-based fans in analyze-sessions.sh or similar still work\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\n- [x] **1. Capture** — done\n- [x] **2. Resource Intelligence** — done\n- [x] **3. Triage** — done\n- [x] **4. Plan Draft** — done\n- [x] **5. User Review - Plan (Draft)** — done\n- [x] **6. Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **7. User Review - Plan (Final)** — done\n- [x] **8. Claim / Activation** — done\n- [x] **9. Work-Queue Routing Skill** — done\n- [x] **10. Work Execution** — done\n- [x] **11. Artifact Generation** — done\n- [x] **12. TDD / Eval** — done\n- [x] **13. Agent Cross-Review** — done\n- [x] **14. Verify Gate Evidence** — done\n- [x] **15. Future Work Synthesis** — done\n- [x] **16. Resource Intelligence Update** — done\n- [x] **17. User Review - Implementation** — done\n- [ ] **18. Reclaim** — n\n- [ ] **19. Close** — pending\n- [ ] **20. Archive** — pending\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/2653","display_title":"WRK-694: Per-session log files in session-logger.sh"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
