{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github_search_issues","arguments":{"repo":"vamseeachanta/workspace-hub","query":"is:issue is:open label:\"status:plan-approved\" created:<2026-04-01","topn":100,"sort":"created","order":"desc"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"issues\": [{\"url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1264\", \"title\": \"WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis\", \"issue_number\": 1264, \"body\": \"## WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis\\n\\n\\n\\n**Status:** pending | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering-calculations | **Subcategory:** structural-dynamics\\n\\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n### Mission\\n\\nBuild a static/quasi-static frame model in OrcaFlex with applied parachute drag force \\u2014 independent verification of 2D and CalculiX results.\\n\\n### What\\n\\n1. **Model frame** as OrcaFlex line objects with correct geometry from WRK-1360\\n2. **Define section properties**: 4130 chromoly tube (OD/wall from CAD), EA/EI/GJ\\n3. **Apply boundary conditions**: fixed supports at vehicle mount points (C3, B1)\\n4. **Apply static drag force** from WRK-1362 at chute attachment point\\n5. **Run static analysis** for all load cases (200/250 MPH)\\n6. **Extract**: member forces, reactions, deflections at key points\\n\\nExecution on **licensed-win-1** (OrcaFlex license required).\\n\\n### Why\\n\\nOrcaFlex provides an independent third-party verification of the frame analysis \\u2014 different solver, different element formulation. Comparing with 2D direct stiffness and CalculiX builds confidence in the results.\\n\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n\\n\\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\\n\\n- [ ] OrcaFlex model built with correct frame geometry and section properties\\n- [ ] Static analysis completed for 200 MPH and 250 MPH load cases\\n- [ ] Member forces and reactions extracted at all support points\\n- [ ] Deflections at chute attachment point reported\\n- [ ] Results exported to YAML for cross-tool comparison (WRK-1366)\\n- [ ] Comparison with 2D/CalculiX results documented (% difference)\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\\n\\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\\n\\nNot yet available\\n\\n</details>\", \"state\": null, \"user\": null, \"assignees\": null, \"labels\": null, \"milestone\": null, \"state_reason\": null, \"comments\": null, \"created_at\": null, \"updated_at\": null, \"closed_at\": null, \"display_url\": \"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1264\", \"display_title\": \"WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis\"}]}"}],"structured_content":{"issues":[{"url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1264","title":"WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis","issue_number":1264,"body":"## WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis\n\n\n\n**Status:** pending | **Priority:** high | **Category:** engineering-calculations | **Subcategory:** structural-dynamics\n\n**Repo:** ['workspace-hub'] | **Complexity:** medium | **Machine:** dev-primary\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n### Mission\n\nBuild a static/quasi-static frame model in OrcaFlex with applied parachute drag force — independent verification of 2D and CalculiX results.\n\n### What\n\n1. **Model frame** as OrcaFlex line objects with correct geometry from WRK-1360\n2. **Define section properties**: 4130 chromoly tube (OD/wall from CAD), EA/EI/GJ\n3. **Apply boundary conditions**: fixed supports at vehicle mount points (C3, B1)\n4. **Apply static drag force** from WRK-1362 at chute attachment point\n5. **Run static analysis** for all load cases (200/250 MPH)\n6. **Extract**: member forces, reactions, deflections at key points\n\nExecution on **licensed-win-1** (OrcaFlex license required).\n\n### Why\n\nOrcaFlex provides an independent third-party verification of the frame analysis — different solver, different element formulation. Comparing with 2D direct stiffness and CalculiX builds confidence in the results.\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n<details><summary>Implementation Summary</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Final Plan</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Acceptance Criteria</summary>\n\n- [ ] OrcaFlex model built with correct frame geometry and section properties\n- [ ] Static analysis completed for 200 MPH and 250 MPH load cases\n- [ ] Member forces and reactions extracted at all support points\n- [ ] Deflections at chute attachment point reported\n- [ ] Results exported to YAML for cross-tool comparison (WRK-1366)\n- [ ] Comparison with 2D/CalculiX results documented (% difference)\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>TDD Results</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Evidence and Cost</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Stage Progress</summary>\n\nNot yet available\n\n</details>","state":null,"user":null,"assignees":null,"labels":null,"milestone":null,"state_reason":null,"comments":null,"created_at":null,"updated_at":null,"closed_at":null,"display_url":"https://github.com/vamseeachanta/workspace-hub/issues/1264","display_title":"WRK-1365: OrcaFlex frame analysis"}]}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
